Woot. Haven't touched nethack for years, but got bored last week and decided
to take a shot at it again. Killed myself on first try (stupid mistake), so I
decided to play it safer with the next character. I wasn't intending to play
it all the way to the end; so at the beginning I was just fooling around and
taking my sweet time to descend the dungeon.

The pet died on Dlvl:1 by some stupid monster (I don't even remember what).
Found a co-aligned altar on Dlvl:2 (woohoo!), and found stairs to Gnomish
Mines on Dlvl:3. I spent quite a long time wandering about these first few
levels, collecting stuff and sacrificing. Descended the Mines rather slowly,
and went up/down between the stash at Dlvl:2 and Minetown many, many times
(and many more times to come later, 'cos I didn't have the intention to finish
the game then, so never bothered to consolidate my loot in one place).

Got Snickersnee, Ogresmasher, and Dragonbane from the altar... and made the
stupid mistake of wasting my enhance points on them rather than saving it for
the Tsurugi (I didn't get it to Expert level with it until I was almost ready
to visit Rodney). Needless to say, I forgot (or didn't know) that all three
weapons were in different classes, so I must've wasted like 6 enhance points
on them.

Anyway, I managed to make it to Mine bottom, and but didn't get the
touchstone. During the journey down to Mine bottom, I lost the splintmail and
a dwarvish mithril coat to two polymorph traps. For some reason, polymorph
seemed to be very prominent at this stage of the game; I got many pots of
polymorph as well as PM wands. I saved the wand for polypiling, but never
ended up using it. Somewhere along the line, I found a cursed lamp, and threw
it away at one point because it wouldn't light. (I forgot that that was
because it was cursed, and mistakenly assumed it was out of oil.) But later
on, through #name'ing, I realized that it was a magic lamp. So I went back to
get it and kept it lit all the way to ascension.

Then I slowly hauled some stuff back to the Dlvl:2 stash, and started making
my way down the main dungeon branch. Found the Oracle at Dlvl:6 (IIRC),
Sokoban at Dlvl:7 (or 8). Did Sokoban, but made mistakes (didn't remember the
right sequence), so I had to pickaxe two boulders to complete it.  I was
hoping for BoH, but got AoR instead, and although I was unhappy with that at
the time, AoR turned out to be immensely useful afterwards. I robbed the shop
on Dlvl:3 and the shopkeeper got mad and fired wands at me (for some reason, I
thought wrongly that standing outside the shop and zapping teleport wands at
shop items did not constitute stealing... lol, who am I kidding) - but thanks
to the AoR, he managed to kill himself doing that.

So I made my way rather slowly down the dungeon, and found another coaligned
altar at Dlvl:11. Stuck around for a long time, sacrificing and making another
stash. (Somewhere around this time, I started to decide that perhaps I'll play
as far as the Castle. I had bad memories of gehennom from previous games, and
didn't feel like I wanted to bother with it. I still had no intention of
ascending this character, you see.) There were lots of treasure zoos below
Dlvl:11, and a beehive or two. Between the royal jelly and a sudden
proliferation of giants, I managed to get my Str up to 18. After a very long
time (going up/down, even making several trips to my minetown stash), I found
the quest portal somewhere around Dlvl:17 or 18, but chickened out and decided
to come back later. Found portal to Fort Ludios at Dlvl:19, and cleared it out
except for the fort itself (didn't get levitation/waterwalking until much
later, and too chicken to use boulders to cross the moat). Got a few more
intrinsics.

Found a non-coaligned altar at Dlvl:22, and converted it. (In retrospect, this
was rather risky since I haven't done the quest yet.) Anyway, I made another
stash here, and made it to Medusa, but didn't have a way to cross the water
and was too chicken to dig down and come back up; so I finally went back and
did the Quest. The nemesis wasn't too hard, as I happened to have a WoD handy.
So I finished the quest (and kicked myself really hard when I realized how
many enhance points I wasted on inferior weapons). Somewhere along the line, I
finally found a BoH, and gathered up the courage to do Medusa. I dug through
to the maze above the castle and climbed back up---and was dumb enough to
forget putting my blindfold on. The AoR came to the rescue again---Medusa
froze herself. So I got the levboots from Perseus' statue, and went back to
sacrifice at Dlvl:22.

Then I went to Fort Ludios and finished it off, and created my red dragon mail
from the scales left by the dead dragons. (In retrospect, I should've waited
until I got grey or silver scales since I already have fire resist intrinsic,
but this worked out OK in the end.) Things seemed to be going quite well now,
but then I made the MOST idiotically stupid mistake: put an unidentified wand
into the BoH. Turned out to be a wand of cancellation. *Poof*. The bag
vanished along with the levboots and many other valuable items. I realized
then that I had to get to the castle and wish for WWboots. So I got ready to
clear out the castle. I managed to clear out the castle and get the WoW, so I
got my WWboots back.

But on the way back to my stash at Dlvl:22, some idiotic monster read a
(cursed) CM scroll, and out popped a master mind flayer in front of me along
with dozens of other monsters. The Tsurugi did him in good; but not before he
sucked my brains out. I forgot a significant number of levels, as well as lots
of scrolls, potions, gems, and even pre-Id's weapons and armor. It was around
this time that I started to consider genociding h's. (Up till then, I managed
pretty good with MF's and MMF's, with my trusty ole yumi. But the risk of
having MMF's pop up next to me when I'm surrounded is more than I'm willing to
take.)

Anyway, I decided that perhaps I was doing well enough that I just might be
able to get the Amulet quickly, so I finally decided to head for ascension. So
I went back to the castle and descended to Gehennom. Pretty soon, I found a
second WoW and found TWO touchstones. Juiblex' lair was only 2 levels below
the Valley, and Asmo and Baalzebub's lairs also followed in quick succession.
Orcus lair was also only 1 or 2 levels away. Juiblex was easy; it engulfed me
and got slit open by the Tsurugi. Asmo got bribed like the fool he is and went
away. Baalzebub gave me some trouble, and managed to flee all the way up to
Juiblex' lair. Orcus was a wimp and fled after first hit, but I blocked the up
stairs with a boulder and did him in good. Anyway, I went looking for Vlad's
tower, but didn't find it, until the first or second levels of Rodney's tower
(I didn't realize it can appear alongside Rodney's tower). At this point I had
AC:-19, so he was no fight. I continued descending, and along the line, I ran
into a gang of master liches and arch liches. Lots of stuff got cursed/
unblessed. I decided that I should genocide L's after wall.

So after another trip to my stash (and genociding L's), I made my way all the
way down to the Vibrating Square at Dlvl:49, left the candelabrum on it, and
went all the way back up clearing the way for my escape later. Sometime along
the way, I clued in to the fact that I had been giving the priest the wrong
amount of money, and so didn't get as much AC as I should. That was quickly
fixed after exhausting my loot from Fort Ludios. (And kicking myself several
times for not doing this earlier when it was cheaper.)

Somewhere in gehennom I found TWO BoH's, in addition to one I wished for to
replace the one that got exploded by the unidentified wand of cancellation. So
this time I went all the way back up to Dlvl:1 and left a BoH there with some
pots, wands, and scrolls needed for the Planes. Then I got everything prepared
for the final run, and made it all the way down to the Vibrating Square, only
to remember that I had forgotten to fetch the bell. (D'oh!) So I had to make
another long trip up to Dlvl:11.

Finally, I entered Rodney's tower and cleared it out... Rodney turned out to
be tougher than I expected, since my WoD's kept on missing him. Finally,
however, I managed to whack him to death with the Tsurugi (but not before he
cursed several items). He appeared again twice on my way to the Sanctum, and
each time the WoD's kept on missing, so I used up most of the charges on it.
The Sanctum was hard at first, but then a cockatrice showed up and left a
carcass, so I turned the place into a museum.

Rodney appeared a few more time on my way up, and the stupid mysterious force
dragged me back several times. But eventually I made it to the Valley and back
up to the Castle, and then ran back up the dungeon. Rodney showed up yet more
times, and this time the WoD's did him in good. Along the way, I picked up the
two WoW's, a number of wands, and made it to the Astral Plane without too many
more setbacks.

The Plane of Earth was hard, 'cos I had limited scrolls and wanted to save the
gold detection scrolls for the dreaded Plane of Air.  It took me a while to
find the portal. I stumbled into the portal quite by accident, but good thing
I had the levboots ready in my inventory. The Plane of Air turned out to be
not as bad as I thought, 'cos I managed to get AC:-31 and HP:375 (from
quaffing the large number of full healing pots I had collected and was too
stingy to use), and so the dreaded AE's didn't hurt me too badly. It took me a
while to find the portal in the Plane of Fire and Plane of Water (and I almost
got drowned in the latter, having forgotten to prepare sufficient long-range
weapons).

But anyway, I finally made it to the Astral Plane, and promptly forgot to give
my guardian angel good armor and good weapons. As a result, he died pretty
soon, and I was left to face the Riders alone. I tried to whack him while
wielding a healing pot, but that seemed to decrease my luck so I gave up. It
didn't last very long anyway. Famine was north, and wasn't too hard to take
care of (I brought along lots of K-rations from Fort Ludios), but it was the
wrong altar. So I did Pestilence on the west (hoping I wouldn't have to face
Death), which proved to be a bit scary, since I was quickly running out of
holy water and the unihorn failed too often. I exhausted all my WoD's here,
but it was still the wrong altar. So I wished for a scroll of charging and
charged up one of the WoD's. That managed to get rid of Pestilence. Now, I
wasn't sure what it takes to survive Death, so I simply waited while orange
dragon in the doorway beat the crap outta me, until one of the priests
summoned insects. Then I carefully moved into the doorway, with 3 priests in
front of me and Death behind them, and stood there while they beat the crap
outta me, until Death wandered off a little and was at a safe enough distance.
Then I carefully hacked my path through the insects, and narrowly escaped
Death. Finally, I reached the right altar and offered the Amulet.


